u32`, `d = p2 >> -one.e` truncated to `c_int`) and the identical `<=` / `>` comparison order; `delta` is taken by value as a mutable copy since C passes the struct by value.\n- **`goto done`** in `js_strtod` became a `'done: { ... break 'done; ... }` labelled block with the endptr/sign epilogue after it.\n- **`errno = ERANGE`** needed a binding not present in `jsi.rs`, so a local `extern \"C\" { fn __errno_location() -> *mut c_int; }` plus `const ERANGE: c_int = 34;` was added at the top of the file (per GUIDE, `jsi.rs` was not edited).\n\n## Build status\n\n`cargo build --release` finishes clean — **no errors and no warnings in `jsdtoa.rs`**. No other file in the repo was touched.\n\n## Differential verification against the C original\n\nRather than only trusting the build, I compiled `c_src/src/jsdtoa.c` with the three entry points renamed (`-Djs_grisu2=c_grisu2`, etc.) and linked it alongside the Rust `libmujs.so`, then compared the two implementations bit-for-bit:\n\n- `js_grisu2`: ~250,000 cases — hand-picked hard values (denormals `5e-324`, `DBL_MAX`, `DBL_MIN`, `1e21`, `1/3`, powers of ten) plus 200,000 random bit patterns. Compared returned length, `*K`, and every output digit.\n- `js_fmtexp`: exponents −400 through 400.\n- `js_strtod`: ~50,000 cases — 30 hand-picked edge cases (empty/garbage input, `1e` with no digits, over/underflowing exponents, `1e2147483647`, 23-digit mantissas, leading whitespace and signs, `.5`, `5.`, `-0`) plus 50,000 random digit/dot/`e` strings. Compared the raw 8 result bytes **and** the returned `endPtr` offset.\n\n**Result: `fails=0`** — zero mismatches in any category. The scratch test directory was removed afterward, so the tree contains only the modified `jsdtoa.rs`.\n\nOne note on a shared edge case rather than a defect: `js_fmtexp` with `e == INT_MIN` negates in place, which is UB in C and wraps in Rust. The crate sets `overflow-checks = false`, so both compile to the same wrapping negation — behaviour is preserved, including the bug. It is unreachable from real exponents in any case.","usage":{"total_tokens":79183,"tool_uses":18,"duration_ms":251923},"uuid":"58db3229-b9ef-49c9-9052-6e45d6326bd5","session_id":"b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd"}
