{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a674085618025575c","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012xg4UTtWkCPMFy24oVxkwW","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-Gl1sJh/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-xM2YSV/b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd/tasks/a674085618025575c.output","summary":"The build is clean. Verification confirms no errors or warnings originating from `regexp.rs`, and the whole crate compiles.\n\n## Summary\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-xM2YSV/translation/src/regexp.rs` now contains the full translation of `c_src/src/regexp.c` plus the types from `regexp.h` (the stub is gone).\n\n**Functions translated: 41**\n- 5 public (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`, signatures kept byte-for-byte from the stub): `js_regcompx`, `js_regfreex`, `js_regcomp`, `js_regfree`, `js_regexec`\n- 36 private `unsafe fn`s: `die` (`-> !`), `canon`, `hex`, `dec`, `isunicodeletter`, `nextrune`, `lexcount`, `newcclass`, `addrange`, `addranges_d/D/s/S/w/W`, `lexclass`, `lex`, `newnode`, `empty`, `newrep`, `regnext`, `regaccept`, `parseatom`, `parserep`, `parsecat`, `parsealt`, `count`, `regemit`, `compile`, `default_alloc` (as `unsafe extern \"C\"` so it fits `js_Alloc`), `isnewline`, `iswordchar`, `incclass`, `incclasscanon`, `strncmpcanon`, `r#match`, and the three `#ifdef TEST` dumpers (`dumpnode`, `dumpcclass`, `dumpprog`, kept for completeness, never called; `main` intentionally omitted since it is a test driver, not library code)\n\n**Types** (all `#[repr(C)]`): `Reprog` (real definition replacing the opaque placeholder), `Reclass`, `Renode`, `Reinst`, and the compiler state `cstate` with `kaboom: [u64; 25]`. `Resub`/`Resub_pair`/`REG_*` come from `jsi.rs` as instructed. Layouts were verified with temporary `const` size assertions (Reinst 32, Renode 32, Reclass 264, Reprog 32, cstate 34192 with `kaboom` at offset 200, 8-aligned); the assertions were then removed.\n\n**Key fidelity points**\n- `_setjmp(addr_of_mut!(g.kaboom))` is called directly in `js_regcompx`, the frame that resumes; `g.pstart`, `g.prog`, and `g.error` are accessed with `setvol!`/`vol!` because they are written after the setjmp and read on the error path. `die` uses `longjmp(..., 1)` and is `-> !`.\n- Allocation goes through the `alloc` callback with the same `size_t`→`int` truncating expressions as C, and the same `default_alloc` (`free` on `n == 0`, else `realloc`).\n- `goto loop` in `compile` became a `loop`/`continue`; the `I_BOL`/`I_EOL` fallthrough-to-`return 1` shape was preserved; `while (n--)` in `strncmpcanon` keeps post-decrement semantics.\n- Deliberately preserved quirks: `strchr(ESCAPES, yychar)` is still called with the raw rune (so a rune whose low byte is 0 still matches the terminator), pointer differences that may involve NULL use `isize` subtraction to give the identical numeric result, and the negative-length `strncmp` conversion matches C's `int`→`size_t`.\n- Only two libc additions were needed: a local `extern \"C\" { fn puts(...) }` for the TEST dumpers; everything else uses `jsi.rs` bindings. No other file was modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":95592,"tool_uses":19,"duration_ms":443705},"uuid":"602a1343-4035-4b72-b6bf-0b8a5b847e6e","session_id":"b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_012xg4UTtWkCPMFy24oVxkwW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build is clean. Verification confirms no errors or warnings originating from `regexp.rs`, and the whole crate compiles.\n\n## Summary\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-xM2YSV/translation/src/regexp.rs` now contains the full translation of `c_src/src/regexp.c` plus the types from `regexp.h` (the stub is gone).\n\n**Functions translated: 41**\n- 5 public (`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`, signatures kept byte-for-byte from the stub): `js_regcompx`, `js_regfreex`, `js_regcomp`, `js_regfree`, `js_regexec`\n- 36 private `unsafe fn`s: `die` (`-> !`), `canon`, `hex`, `dec`, `isunicodeletter`, `nextrune`, `lexcount`, `newcclass`, `addrange`, `addranges_d/D/s/S/w/W`, `lexclass`, `lex`, `newnode`, `empty`, `newrep`, `regnext`, `regaccept`, `parseatom`, `parserep`, `parsecat`, `parsealt`, `count`, `regemit`, `compile`, `default_alloc` (as `unsafe extern \"C\"` so it fits `js_Alloc`), `isnewline`, `iswordchar`, `incclass`, `incclasscanon`, `strncmpcanon`, `r#match`, and the three `#ifdef TEST` dumpers (`dumpnode`, `dumpcclass`, `dumpprog`, kept for completeness, never called; `main` intentionally omitted since it is a test driver, not library code)\n\n**Types** (all `#[repr(C)]`): `Reprog` (real definition replacing the opaque placeholder), `Reclass`, `Renode`, `Reinst`, and the compiler state `cstate` with `kaboom: [u64; 25]`. `Resub`/`Resub_pair`/`REG_*` come from `jsi.rs` as instructed. Layouts were verified with temporary `const` size assertions (Reinst 32, Renode 32, Reclass 264, Reprog 32, cstate 34192 with `kaboom` at offset 200, 8-aligned); the assertions were then removed.\n\n**Key fidelity points**\n- `_setjmp(addr_of_mut!(g.kaboom))` is called directly in `js_regcompx`, the frame that resumes; `g.pstart`, `g.prog`, and `g.error` are accessed with `setvol!`/`vol!` because they are written after the s