` is the benign case.\n- **`goto loop` / `goto end`** in `Sp_replace_regexp` became a `loop { ... }` inside a `'end: { ... }` labelled block, with `continue` for `goto loop` and `break 'end` for `goto end`.\n- **`switch` fallthrough** (`case 0: --r; /* fallthrough */ case '$':`) replicated explicitly in both `$`-substitution chains; the `$1`..`$9`, `$&`, `` $` ``, `$'`, `$$` logic including the two-digit path and the original `if (x > 10)` off-by-one (rather than `>= 10`) is preserved verbatim.\n- **regexp**: `(*re).prog` cast with `as *mut crate::regexp::Reprog`; `Resub` locals use `core::mem::zeroed()` (C leaves them uninitialised, but `js_regexec` initialises all `REG_MAXSUB` entries before use).\n- `EOF` declared as a file-local `const c_int = -1` (matching the private consts in `regexp.rs`/`jslex.rs`, so no glob-export clash).\n- All error messages, buffer sizes (`UTFmax + 1`, `(top-1) * UTFmax + 1`, `UTFmax + (tail - head)`), the `JS_STRLIMIT` checks and their ordering are unchanged.\n\n## Build status\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles the whole crate successfully; the verification grep for `jsstring` returns no matches, i.e. **zero errors and zero warnings in `jsstring.rs`**.\n\nOne note on verification: the first few `cargo build` invocations reported `Finished ... in 0.01s` without recompiling, because a concurrent cargo process held the build-directory lock and had already produced the artifact. I re-ran with `touch src/jsstring.rs` to force a genuine recompile of the module and confirm the clean result — worth knowing if you see the same suspiciously fast \"Finished\" line elsewhere in this workspace.","usage":{"total_tokens":90093,"tool_uses":19,"duration_ms":275656},"uuid":"9c3f10a6-261b-4ca7-b1f3-b2ae2a20c518","session_id":"b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd"}
