{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a3bb9b792136f0c2c","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Cn7y1f7PsJtanTgcUkRA2R","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-Gl1sJh/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-xM2YSV/b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd/tasks/a3bb9b792136f0c2c.output","summary":"Build is clean. Summary:\n\n**Done:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-xM2YSV/translation/src/jsdate.rs` now contains the full translation of `c_src/src/jsdate.c` (861 lines C → ~830 lines Rust), replacing the stub.\n\n**Functions translated: 77** — all C definitions in the file are present (verified: 77 C function definitions vs. 77 translated Rust functions plus one helper, see below):\n- Time/spec helpers: `Now`, `LocalTZA` (with the function-local `static mut once/tza`), `DaylightSavingTA`, `pmod`, `Day`, `TimeWithinDay`, `DaysInYear`, `DayFromYear`, `TimeFromYear`, `YearFromTime`, `InLeapYear`, `DayWithinYear`, `MonthFromTime`, `DateFromTime`, `WeekDay`, `LocalTime`, `UTC`, `HourFromTime`, `MinFromTime`, `SecFromTime`, `msFromTime`, `MakeTime`, `MakeDay` (with the 2×12 `firstDayOfMonth` table), `MakeDate`, `TimeClip`\n- Parsing/formatting: `toint`, `parseDateTime`, `fmtdate`, `fmttime`, `fmtdatetime` (exact `sprintf` format strings, `char buf[20]`/`[64]` buffer sizes preserved, `\"Invalid Date\"` early returns kept in original order — i.e. after the `YearFromTime`/`HourFromTime` computations, as in C)\n- `js_todate`, `js_setdate`, `D_parse`, `D_UTC`, `D_now`, `jsB_Date`, `jsB_new_Date`, all 6 `Dp_to*String`/`valueOf`, all 17 getters, all 15 setters, `Dp_toJSON`, and `jsB_initdate` (property table order, names and arity identical; callbacks passed as `Some(fn)`).\n\n**Notable translation decisions:**\n- `js_optnumber(J,I,V)` became a local `macro_rules!` so the default expression stays lazily evaluated like the C ternary.\n- C's implicit `double → int` conversions (in `Day`, `DayFromYear`, `YearFromTime`, `WeekDay`, `HourFromTime`/`MinFromTime`/`SecFromTime`/`msFromTime`, `MakeDay`'s `(int)m` and `DaysInYear(y)`/`TimeFromYear(y)`, and `parseDateTime`'s `int tza`) go through a tiny `d2i()` helper that reproduces x86-64 `cvttsd2si` semantics (NaN / out-of-range → `INT_MIN`). A plain `as c_int` would have silently produced `0` for NaN, which is observably different: e.g. `d = new Date(NaN); d.setMilliseconds(5)` yields `NaN` in C but a valid timestamp with Rust's saturating cast. This is the only added function.\n- Int arithmetic that can overflow on the `INT_MIN` path (`365*(y-1970)`, `y-1969`, `Day(t)+4`, `Day(t)-DayFromYear(...)`, `++y/--y`) uses `wrapping_*`.\n- Preserved the upstream bug in `Dp_setUTCHours` where the minutes default is `HourFromTime(t)` rather than `MinFromTime(t)`, and `fmtdatetime` ignoring the return values of `fmtdate`/`fmttime`.\n- No extra `extern \"C\"` block was needed; `time`, `gettimeofday`, `localtime`, `gmtime`, `mktime`, `floor`, `fmod`, `fabs`, `sprintf` all come from `jsi.rs`.\n\n**Build status:** `cargo build --release` completes with **zero errors and zero warnings attributable to `src/jsdate.rs`** (`grep -A12 jsdate` over a forced rebuild of the file returns nothing); the whole crate finishes building.","usage":{"total_tokens":78355,"tool_uses":15,"duration_ms":308713},"uuid":"a99757f5-c94b-432a-ab23-8a00379bddf2","session_id":"b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd"}
