{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yzojqnxcxap3gob4ndaz4zi3otpw25xgfmmtjxwp7gpiab7jnpbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Result\n\n`translation/` contains a full Rust cdylib translation of the entire MuJS 1.3.8 C library (all 25 `.c` files + 4 headers, ~16k lines C → **20,571 lines of Rust** in 32 modules).\n\n**Symbol parity:** `nm -D` on the Rust `.so` exports exactly the same **237** symbols as the C `.so` — `diff` of the two lists is empty (verified after a clean `rm -rf target && cargo build --release`, 0 warnings).\n\n**Differential testing** (C and Rust `.so` are drop-in swappable behind one C driver binary):\n\n| suite | comparisons | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| C API surface (every `mujs.h` function) | 1 × 5 modes | byte-identical |\n| internal exports (`jsU_*`, `js_grisu2`, `js_strtod`, `jsV_numberto*`, `jsY_*`, `js_itoa`, `js_intern`, …) | 1241 lines | identical |\n| raw `js_regcomp/regexec/regfree` matrix (flags × patterns × texts) | 2820 lines | identical |\n| 16 hand-written JS suites (numbers, strings, objects, arrays, control flow, JSON/repr, Date local+UTC, Math, RegExp, errors, limits, `debugger`/`js_trap`, `jsS_dumpstrings`, syntax-error battery) × 5 modes (default/strict/dumpstrings/runlimit/memlimit) | — | identical |\n| 2500 random expressions, 2500 random regexps (27,916 lines), 120 random generated programs | — | identical |\n| variadic `js_error`/`js_typeerror`/… called from C with mixed `%s %d %g`, 10 int args, stack spill | — | identical |\n| **total** | **485 file comparisons + extras** | **all byte-identical, same exit codes** |\n\nEven `js_gc(J,1)` report lines match exactly (identical env/fun/obj/prop/str allocation counts), and `jsS_dumpstrings` reproduces the same AA-tree shape — strong evidence the internal data structures behave identically, not just the observable output.\n\n**Notable engineering points**\n- `js_State`, `js_Value`, `js_Object`, `js_Property`, `js_Jumpbuf`, … are `#[repr(C)]` with compile-time `assert!`s pinning them to the C sizes (`js_State` == 48552 bytes, etc.).\n- Exceptions use the real `_setjmp`/`longjmp`, with `vol!`/`setvol!` volatile access wherever the C used `volatile` across a `longjmp`.\n- The 8 public **variadic** functions (impossible to define in stable Rust) are implemented by reconstructing the SysV x86-64 `va_list` from register/stack parameters and handing it to libc `vsnprintf` — ABI-verified against the C library.\n- All formatting/IO goes through libc (`printf`, `snprintf`, `fputs`) so bytes and buffering match; C bugs (e.g. `Dp_setUTCHours` using `HourFromTime` for minutes, `jsM_round`'s integer `-0`, the truncated `\"[iterator \"` repr, the `'\\'` token-table fold) are preserved deliberately.\n\nTest harness left in `dtest/` (`dtest/run.sh` re-runs everything); the C reference build is in `_cbuild/`; conventions used by the translation are documented in `GUIDE.md`. `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4103,"cache_read_input_tokens":398817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4103,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5f4468e-76fc-4f11-a872-3a6ebded8ecd","uuid":"d6075b02-73ec-42c8-90b7-afe7c925770f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:35:43.542Z"}
